.TH H2PLAYER "1" "July 23, 2026" "Hydrogen 2.0.0-pre-alpha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
h2player \- headless Hydrogen song player with IPC server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBh2player\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI*.h2song\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBh2player\fR can play a song created with \fBHydrogen\fR without starting its
GUI. By default, it starts an IPC server that allows the Hydrogen GUI to
connect and control playback remotely. The GUI can be attached manually using
the \fBhydrogen -c\fR command.
.PP
You start \fBh2player\fR using a particular song (\fI*.h2song\fR), project (\fI*.h2project\fR), or playlist (\fI*.h2playlist\fR) file. It will use all its
solo/mute settings as well as transport settings from your last Hydrogen
session.
.SH MODES
.TP
\fBDefault mode\fR
Starts IPC server and prints connection information. The Hydrogen GUI can be
connected manually using the \fBhydrogen -c\fR command. Runs an event loop to
handle IPC communication.
.TP
\fBInteractive mode\fR (\fB--interactive\fR)
Keyboard-controlled mode with simple commands: play (p), stop (s), rewind (b),
show frame (f), debug (d), quit (q). Can be combined with IPC server for
simultaneous keyboard and GUI control.
.TP
\fBNo-IPC mode\fR (\fB--no-ipc\fR)
Disables IPC server for pure headless operation. Useful for automation and
testing where no external control is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
Enable keyboard-interactive mode.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-no-ipc\fR
Disable IPC server (pure headless mode).
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-driver\fR=[\fIAUDIO_DRIVER\fR]
Use the selected audio driver. The description of this option in the -\-help output contains all audio
drivers available on your system.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-kit\fR=\fIDRUMKIT_NAME\fR
Load a drumkit at startup.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR=[\fILEVEL\fR]
Print a lot of debugging info
.IP
Level, if present, may be \fINone\fR, \fIError\fR, \fIWarning\fR, \fIInfo\fR, \fIDebug\fR, or \fIIpc\fR.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-log\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Use custom log file.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-log\-timestamps\fR
Add timestamps to all log messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-colors\fR
Use ANSI colors in log messages (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-log\-colors\fR
Suppress ANSI colors in log messages.
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-data\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate system data path.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\-data\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate user data path.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate path to the \fIhydrogen.conf\fR file.
.TP
\fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-osc\-port\fR=\fIPORT\fR
Use custom OSC port.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version info.
.SH IPC CONNECTION
.PP
By default, h2player starts an IPC server and prints connection information:
.PP
.nf
  ========================================
  IPC Server Started
  ========================================
  Endpoint: hydrogen-headless-1234-0

  To connect the Hydrogen GUI, run:
    hydrogen -c hydrogen-headless-1234-0
    hydrogen --connect-via-ipc hydrogen-headless-1234-0

  Press Ctrl+C to stop the server
  ========================================
.fi
.PP
To connect the GUI, run the displayed command in another terminal. The GUI will
attach to the running h2player instance and provide full visual control.
.SH KEYBOARD COMMANDS
.PP
In interactive mode, the following keyboard commands are available:
.IP
.B b
\- Rewind to the beginning of the song.
.IP
.B p
\- Start playback.
.IP
.B s
\- Stop playback.
.IP
.B f
\- Show the current transport position in frames.
.IP
.B d
\- Show debug information (object count).
.IP
.B q
\- Quit h2player.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Command-line syntax error.
.TP
2
Song file loading error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start h2player with IPC server (default):
.RS
.PP
h2player mysong.h2song
.RE
.PP
Start h2player in interactive mode:
.RS
.PP
h2player mysong.h2song --interactive
.RE
.PP
Start h2player without IPC server:
.RS
.PP
h2player mysong.h2song --no-ipc
.RE
.PP
Connect GUI to running h2player:
.RS
.PP
# In terminal 1:
h2player mysong.h2song
.PP
# In terminal 2:
hydrogen -c <endpoint-from-terminal-1>
.RE
